ritain outscored her opponents by 17-2."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Great Britain was led by " [:a {:href "/athletes/18860"} "Stanley Shoveller"] ", the island nation’s greatest ever center-forward, who captained the English side from 1910-1921.  In the match against Belgium, Shoveller scored 6 goals.  Shoveller had also played for the English team that had won the " [:a {:href "/results/35500"} "1908 hockey"] " gold medal.  He was the only player who competed in hockey at both the 1908 and 1920 Olympic Games."] "\n\n" [:p {} "One of the British players, " [:a {:href "/athletes/1006095"} "Rex Crummack"] ", was far better known as a golfer.  He played in the British Amateur Championship in 1909 and continued through 1946, the only player to have competed before World War I and after World War II.  Another, " [:a {:href "/athletes/18816"} "Jack MacBryan"] ", was a well known cricketer, being named in 1925 as one of Wisden’s Cricketers of the Year."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button971005", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button971005').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {}] [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Team"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Games Played", :class "split", :style "display: none"} "GP"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Goals"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {:class "accordion-toggle", :data-toggle "collapse", :data-target ".team-members-510724"} [:div {:class "glyphicon glyphicon-plus"}]] [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class " accordion-body team-membe